From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: MAINTAINERS: cover shared memory hotplug headers
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:30:41 -0800

Cover firmware memory-map updates, node registration and memory-block
associations, plus memory-hotplug notification failure injection. The
firmware interface is shared with MEMBLOCK AND INITIALIZATION; the node
interface is also assigned to NUMA PLACEMENT by the next patch.

Add the following file assignments:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - MEMORY HOT(UN)PLUG
        include/linux/firmware-map.h
        include/linux/node.h
        lib/memory-notifier-error-inject.c

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Oscar Salvador <osalvador@suse.de>
---

 MAINTAINERS |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/MAINTAINERS~maintainers-cover-shared-memory-hotplug-headers
+++ a/MAINTAINERS
@@ -17525,8 +17525,11 @@ F:	Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-devic
 F:	Documentation/admin-guide/mm/memory-hotplug.rst
 F:	Documentation/core-api/memory-hotplug.rst
 F:	drivers/base/memory.c
+F:	include/linux/firmware-map.h
 F:	include/linux/memory_hotplug.h
